Privacy Policy — Scam Check Malaysia

Effective Date: 6 October 2026

Scam Check Malaysia (“ScamCheck”, “we”, “our”, or “us”) operates the Scam Check Android application and related website (the “App”).

IMPORTANT: ScamCheck is an independent public-interest tool. It is NOT a government application and is NOT operated by, affiliated with, endorsed by, or representing the Government of Malaysia, PDRM, Bank Negara Malaysia, Securities Commission Malaysia, SSM, Ministry of Health Malaysia, NSRC, or any other government agency.

This Privacy Policy explains how we handle information when you use the App.

1. Information We Collect

a) Public verification checks
When you check a website, phone number, bank account, company, investment name, or product name, that input is used only to produce the verification result for that request. We do not keep public checks as search history.

b) Community reports (optional)
If you submit a community report, you provide report details and consent. That submitted report may be stored for moderation and public-interest display. Reporting is separate from a normal check.

c) Technical / device information
The App may process limited technical data needed to run the service (for example, basic request handling, rate limiting, or crash/stability information if enabled by the platform). We do not sell personal data.

d) What we do not intentionally collect for advertising
We do not require an account for public checks and do not intentionally collect government IDs for advertising profiles.

2. How We Use Information
• Provide verification results against public/official source lists and curated references
• Moderate community reports when submitted with consent
• Improve reliability, security, and abuse prevention (including rate limits)
• Respond to support requests

3. Data Storage
• Public check inputs are processed to return a result and are not retained as searchable user history
• Community reports are stored only when explicitly submitted with consent
• Admin configuration and operational data may be stored on our servers (for example Firebase/Google Cloud) to run the service

4. Data Sharing
We do not sell, rent, or trade user data.
Data may be disclosed only:
• To infrastructure providers needed to operate the App (for example Google Play / Firebase / hosting)
• When required by law

5. Third-Party / Official Sources
The App may query or reference third-party and government public sources. Those sources have their own terms and privacy practices. Opening an official portal link means you are subject to that portal’s policy.

6. Data Security
We take reasonable measures to protect systems and data, but no method is 100% secure.

7. Your Choices
• You can stop using the App or uninstall it at any time
• For community-report questions or deletion requests related to a report you submitted, contact us

8. Children’s Privacy
The App is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.

9. Changes
We may update this Privacy Policy. The Effective Date above will be revised when changes are published.

